AUDIO: 'Adobe Premiere is getting optimized from the ground up to take advantage of NVIDIA TRT RTX acceleration, which means features and effects will run incredibly fast on RTX Spark. Here we have two identical RTX Spark laptops, one running the standard Adobe Premiere, and one'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'running our TRT RTX optimized version of Premiere. How about we start with scene edit detection? We can see that the accelerated version here performs faster, allowing editors to quickly identify and modify cut points within an exported clip.'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There\'s also a new color mode with a 32-bit float GPU pipeline, which accelerates the user interface for real-time color correction. And in addition, there\'s also a new feature within Premiere called object mask tool,'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'which allows us to track an object with one click, significantly faster than our previous version of Premiere. Playback and editing a multi-cam 4K 10-bit 422 60 frames per second footage is very processor intensive, and used to'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'require transcodes or low-resolution proxies just for playback. But with NVIDIA hardware acceleration, we can now playback multiple streams simultaneously. This is what it looks like when the hardware and software are'

[01:01] [scene:talk]
